MID_EV12_045_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_045_m01_001: Reports of the defeat of Cetus, the Sea Tyrant, have\nreached me. Well done.
MID_EV12_045_m01_002: The soldiers who accompanied you, even the \nbravest of the generals, spoke of its fearsomeness.
MID_EV12_045_m01_003: I hear you and your companions fought tenaciously\nand with great strength.
MID_EV12_045_m01_004: I could see it in their eyes as they regaled me with\ntales of your valor... You have won them over.
MID_EV12_045_m01_005: *sigh*
MID_EV12_045_m01_006: You have done the empire a great service.
MID_EV12_045_m01_007: And in recognition of that, you must be rewarded\nin kind.
MID_EV12_045_m01_008: Tell me! What do you wish? I will grant whatever is\nin my power. Now or later, I would hear of it.
MID_EV12_045_m01_009: I joined the Heroic Games so that I might\ndefeat Cetus.
MID_EV12_045_m01_010: But now that I have...I have a new aim.
MID_EV12_045_m01_011: What would that be? Do tell!
MID_EV12_045_m01_012: Once I have achieved victory in the Heroic Games, I\nwill reveal it to you.
MID_EV12_045_m01_013: I see. Very well. As ever, you confound expectations.
MID_EV12_045_m01_014: To slay a beast so fierce it was known as the Sea\nTyrant... What an exploit!
MID_EV12_045_m01_015: I did not believe a human could accomplish this. You\nhave my apologies.
MID_EV12_045_m01_016: As the soldiers regaled us with the tale, Mars was\nmoved to jealousy.
MID_EV12_045_m01_017: Mars, the god of war? That does remind me...
MID_EV12_045_m01_018: A warrior so mighty would surely wish to face such\na beast.
MID_EV12_045_m01_019: I find it strange that he never himself fought Cetus.
MID_EV12_045_m01_020: There is a very simple reason. Mars cannot swim.
MID_EV12_045_m01_021: He nearly drowned as a child, and so avoids\nthe water.
MID_EV12_045_m01_022: Lord Solel... That is, perhaps, indiscreet...
MID_EV12_045_m01_023: You're right, Anna. Please, Dietrich. Do not share\nthis information.
MID_EV12_045_m01_024: I do not wish to injure my brother's dignity.
MID_EV12_045_m01_025: I swear that I will tell no one. My sister cannot swim\neither, so I sympathize.
MID_EV12_045_m01_026: I appreciate it. I shall guard her secret as well.
MID_EV12_045_m01_027: About the Heroic Games... Matches will resume\nin Seftim.
MID_EV12_045_m01_028: As regards your next opponent, however, that battle\nis scheduled for Oxum.
MID_EV12_045_m01_029: You have some time to fill. Fill it well.
MID_EV12_046_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_046_m01_001: Welcome back. How did you fare this time?
MID_EV12_046_m01_002: All is well. The Divine Sovereign wishes to reward\nme for defeating Cetus. We will discuss it later.
MID_EV12_046_m01_003: And we shared a few secrets.
MID_EV12_046_m01_004: Hm? Well, alright.
MID_EV12_046_m01_005: Now, about our destination. Have you identified it?
MID_EV12_046_m01_006: I have. At least roughly, based on the information I\nreceived from Hannibal.
MID_EV12_046_m01_007: It is far to the west of the Chronos Desert, in\nthe Nysiades region. Fezzan.
MID_EV12_046_m01_008: Supposedly there is a giant wall cordoning off a\nsection of the desert. Something must lie beyond it.
MID_EV12_046_m01_009: It is said to be the forbidden land. That is\nmy target.
MID_EV12_046_m01_010: Forbidden land? How enticing.
MID_EV12_046_m01_011: As I investigated, I uncovered something interesting.
MID_EV12_046_m01_012: It is known as the legend of the White Egg.
MID_EV12_046_m01_013: It tells of a huge white egg in the desert sand, in\nwhich people, perhaps celestials, dwelt.
MID_EV12_046_m01_014: These people battled Dagda the Great. The egg was\ncracked, and they were taken prisoner.
MID_EV12_046_m01_015: After that, a wall was erected around it, and none\ncould gain entry again. Those are the broad strokes.
MID_EV12_046_m01_016: This legend, when paired with the information I\nreceived from Hannibal, led me to a conclusion.
MID_EV12_046_m01_017: What I seek must exist even now. The empire itself\nonce encountered it, after all.
MID_EV12_046_m01_018: And while the White Egg was laid to waste by Dagda\nthe Great, something must remain.
MID_EV12_046_m01_019: There is also the matter of Anatolia and her\ncompanions. I am certain they are connected.
MID_EV12_046_m01_020: Very well.
MID_EV12_046_m01_021: So our destination must be this desert. It will\nbe harsh.
MID_EV12_046_m01_022: We may also be unable to find supplies there, so we\nmust prepare before we set out.
MID_EV12_046_m01_023: This reminds me. Did you not receive permission to\nuse the Gate of the Gods at Mars's temple?
MID_EV12_046_m01_024: That would shorten our journey considerably.
MID_EV12_046_m01_025: You recall the gated wall standing in the desert, do\nyou not? That is our objective.
MID_EV12_047_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_047_m01_001: It is, in a word, imposing. I had not expected it to be\nso vast.
MID_EV12_047_m01_002: What a formidable edifice... Dagda the Great must\nhave truly feared what it contained.
MID_EV12_047_m01_003: It's huge, sure. But if you wanted to get out, I think\nyou could.
MID_EV12_047_m01_004: The bricks are rough. I bet there are plenty of\nhandholds for climbing.
MID_EV12_047_m01_005: Even if you can't get the gate open, you could\nstill just climb over.
MID_EV12_047_m01_006: Sure, but how would they bring out supplies? Think\nabout livestock.
MID_EV12_047_m01_007: Just so. As you must have learned from our journey\nhere, this place is all but devoid of life.
MID_EV12_047_m01_008: To roam around this waste empty-handed would\nspell doom.
MID_EV12_047_m01_009: There should be soldiers patrolling as well.
MID_EV12_047_m01_010: Were someone to climb the wall, those soldiers would\nsurely spot them.
MID_EV12_047_m01_011: The People of the White Egg are the stuff of legends.\nThey're said to have incredible power.
MID_EV12_047_m01_012: Even now, if you see one of them, you're supposed to\nreport them to a temple.
MID_EV12_047_m01_013: There's a folk belief they all wear white. It's been\npassed down forever.
MID_EV12_047_m01_014: I've seen travelers stopped and questioned just\nfor that.
MID_EV12_047_m01_015: It is good our clothes do not arouse such suspicions.
MID_EV12_047_m01_016: Maybe not those suspicions, but you two look\nso out of place in Dagda... *sigh*
MID_EV12_047_m01_017: Anyway, folk get jumpy. They think the People of\nthe White Egg will take their revenge.
MID_EV12_047_m01_018: Revenge? For what?
MID_EV12_047_m01_019: It's an old tale. One hundred thousand of the People\nof the White Egg were dragged to Dagsion and killed.
MID_EV12_047_m01_020: The tale is that they were boiled to death in\nsomething called Dagda's cauldron.
MID_EV12_047_m01_021: My parents used to use it to scare me. "Be good, or\nDagda the Great will boil you up!"
MID_EV12_047_m01_022: Have you seen a giant cauldron in Dagsion?
MID_EV12_047_m01_023: Maybe it's all made up, or at least got exaggerated\nover the years.
MID_EV12_047_m01_024: Boiling thousands of people alive in a cauldron\nsounds farfetched, if you ask me.
MID_EV12_047_m01_025: Who could even build a cauldron big enough? Or\na lid for it?
MID_EV12_047_m01_026: {SetColor=Gray}Some things are too large to lie about.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_047_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}Fascinating to suppose for a moment it did exist...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_047_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}Yet to simply execute people, there is no need to\nbuild something so vulgar and ostentatious.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_047_m01_029: {SetColor=Gray}Perhaps its grandeur was to cow the masses? Or\nperhaps it was used to process the condemned...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_048_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_048_m01_001: Ohhh.
MID_EV12_048_m01_002: What IS this? A giant egg?
MID_EV12_048_m01_003: The size of this thing is no joke. And like the legends\nsay, this egg is thoroughly cracked.
MID_EV12_048_m01_004: <NCA>Look at the White Egg.
MID_EV12_048_m01_005: <NCB>Look at Fabio.
MID_EV12_048_m01_006: <ACA>Do I sight residences in that structure? It appears\nmost of them have been destroyed.
MID_EV12_048_m01_007: <ACA>Yet traces suggest inhabitants even now... This is\na dwelling.
MID_EV12_048_m01_008: <ACA>It's huge! Huger than I'd imagined from the stories. It\nmight be bigger than Dagsion.
MID_EV12_048_m01_009: <ACB>The wreckage of an Echidna-class vessel... It is as\nI anticipated.
MID_EV12_048_m01_010: <ACB>The residential sector's dome has sustained heavy\ndamage and caved in. Cracked egg, indeed.
MID_EV12_048_m01_011: <ACB>It is in even worse condition than I'd imagined.\nThere is no hope for it.
MID_EV12_048_m01_012: Hey, look over there! I see some kids.
MID_EV12_048_m01_013: Who...who are you?
MID_EV12_048_m01_014: Help! Outsiders! They're trying to get in!
MID_EV12_048_m01_015: Hey! You kids! Wait! And they're gone.
MID_EV12_048_m01_016: This doesn't look good. What do you want?
MID_EV12_048_m01_017: They're serious—deadly serious. I don't think they're\nhere for a chat.
MID_EV12_048_m01_018: A pleasure to meet you. I am Anacharsis of Agartha.\nI would speak with the representative of Nuwa.
MID_EV12_048_m01_019: *murmur*
MID_EV12_048_m01_020: I am Zenon, captain of Nuwa. You are the one who\nhas made contact with the Grand Megaliths.
MID_EV12_048_m01_021: Katarina sent me a report. It seems you've been\ntraveling this land for some years now.
MID_EV12_048_m01_022: How did you make your way here, follower of Vritra?\nWhat led you to us?
MID_EV12_048_m01_023: We challenged Hannibal and won. The spoils of our\nvictory were information about this place.
MID_EV12_048_m01_024: Unthinkable... Such a paltry thing motivated the\nGrand Megalith to aid you?
MID_EV12_048_m01_025: You might call it a glitch in the machine. To get what\nI wanted, I exploited it.
MID_EV12_048_m01_026: Each quantum computing device was given its own\npersonality, to foster different perspectives.
MID_EV12_048_m01_027: This, it was thought, would lead to robust decisions,\nmade by different personalities working in concert.
MID_EV12_048_m01_028: Personally, I had my doubts about the approach. But\nI certainly was able to take advantage of it.
MID_EV12_048_m01_029: And now—what do you intend?
MID_EV12_048_m01_030: I will report your location to Vritra. That is the\nmission I was entrusted.
MID_EV12_048_m01_031: Pity. We cannot permit any of Vritra's followers\nto leave here alive.
MID_EV12_048_m01_032: I see. A shame it is indeed. Having been warned,\nhowever, we will decline to comply.
MID_EV12_048_m01_033: Dietrich! It is time for your turn upon the stage!
MID_EV12_048_m01_034: At long last. Those who wish to die—come forth.
MID_EV12_049_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_049_m01_001: This is as far as we go, eh? I had hoped we would\nfare better, given our opponents were few.
MID_EV12_049_m01_002: We have no particular desire to claim your lives.\nNow, tell me something.
MID_EV12_049_m01_003: What is Nuwa doing in this place? Our records state\nthe ship was lost. 
MID_EV12_049_m01_004: Ah...
MID_EV12_049_m01_005: That day, with one million aboard, we lingered in\norbit, waiting to depart.
MID_EV12_049_m01_006: We gazed upon the planet from the distant sky...as\nthat thing assaulted it.
MID_EV12_049_m01_007: Captain! There's... There's some kind of attack! What\nis it?
MID_EV12_049_m01_008: Oh! It is calamity itself.
MID_EV12_049_m01_009: Are we being punished for reaching toward space?\nFor exceeding our reach? For our hubris?
MID_EV12_049_m01_010: But... What is it? Where did it come from?
MID_EV12_049_m01_011: Our defenses should have detected it on\nplanetary approach!
MID_EV12_049_m01_012: Correct. They would have. Even teleportation would\nproduce gravitational waves.
MID_EV12_049_m01_013: But what if it didn't just arrive? What if it has been\nhere all along?
MID_EV12_049_m01_014: If that is true... No wonder we didn't detect\nits approach.
MID_EV12_049_m01_015: There was nothing we could have done.
MID_EV12_049_m01_016: When humanity exited the stone age, how did we\nmake the leap?
MID_EV12_049_m01_017: The flood that swallowed the world... The flames of\njudgment that fell upon it... The giant that shaped it...
MID_EV12_049_m01_018: The world is full of myths, isn't it? Perhaps this thing\nhad a role in some of them.
MID_EV12_049_m01_019: Humanity held dominion over the planet. We had\nno doubts about our superiority.
MID_EV12_049_m01_020: But, what if that thing has been here all along,\ninfluencing our very civilization?
MID_EV12_049_m01_021: Captain! Crafts 16 and 17, Kukulcan and\nLeviathan, on target for impact!
MID_EV12_049_m01_022: Both ships, direct hit! Ships...lost. The target is\nreeling. It's working!
MID_EV12_049_m01_023: You can't mean—has Vritra ordered a suicide attack?
MID_EV12_049_m01_024: Captain! Orders from Vritra. We're to ram the target\nwith the Nuwa, like the others!
MID_EV12_049_m01_025: Captain... Should we... Can we...
MID_EV12_049_m01_026: Tch... Grr.
MID_EV12_049_m01_027: Vritra instructed the ships to engage their sub-\nlight-speed engines and sacrifice themselves.
MID_EV12_049_m01_028: It was, in fact, the only gambit that had any effect.\nAnd, indeed, it was remarkable in its efficacy.
MID_EV12_049_m01_029: We surmise that Vritra concluded that three ships\nwould be required to silence the target.
MID_EV12_049_m01_030: Kukulcan, Leviathan, and Nuwa.
MID_EV12_049_m01_031: But in the end, Nuwa did not engage.
MID_EV12_049_m01_032: If it had, humanity may well have been victorious.
MID_EV12_049_m01_033: To this day, the name Nuwa is cursed by Agartha.
MID_EV12_049_m01_034: *sigh*
MID_EV12_049_m01_035: The records state that Nuwa was destroyed on\natmospheric reentry—shattered and lost.
MID_EV12_049_m01_036: Yet here it lies. Fascinating. Now how did\nthat happen?
MID_EV12_049_m01_037: Come with me, visitor of Agartha. I will reveal\nthe answer.
MID_EV12_050_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_050_m01_001: Behold. The quantum computing device Chang'e.\nShe is the mind of Nuwa.
MID_EV12_050_m01_002: She? Then this megalith has the personality of\na woman.
MID_EV12_050_m01_003: Precisely. And she is like a mother to all of us in the\nvillage of Kunlun.
MID_EV12_050_m01_004: Her capability was once on the same scale as those\nGrand Megaliths scattered across the world...
MID_EV12_050_m01_005: Having sustained repeated damage, however, she\nmaintains less than 10 percent functionality.
MID_EV12_050_m01_006: That day, she determined the safety of the people on\nthe ship took precedence over Vritra's orders.
MID_EV12_050_m01_007: Her feint was to appear to carry out her orders—and\nthen deconstruct the ship as it fell to the ground.
MID_EV12_050_m01_008: It appeared as though Nuwa had broken up in the\natmosphere. But it crash-landed here, in the desert.
MID_EV12_050_m01_009: The whim of a machine. Another glitch, so to speak.
MID_EV12_050_m01_010: Foolhardy to see it as a mother's love.
MID_EV12_050_m01_011: <NCA>Look at Fabio.
MID_EV12_050_m01_012: <NCB>Look at Mikaela.
MID_EV12_050_m01_013: <ACA>If Vritra were to learn that Nuwa held survivors,\nthey would be eradicated—without hesitation.
MID_EV12_050_m01_014: <ACA>Yes. More than anything, we feared Vritra learning\nof our existence.
MID_EV12_050_m01_015: <ACA>When the world was thrown into chaos, we used that\nchance to take control of the Grand Megaliths.
MID_EV12_050_m01_016: <ACA>We studied them, repaired them, learned to modify\nthem, and then disconnected them from Vritra.
MID_EV12_050_m01_017: <ACA>And so we were able to make lives in Kunlun, hidden\nfrom prying eyes.
MID_EV12_050_m01_018: <ACA>For Agartha and Vritra, this vast land of Dagda had\nbeen a total mystery, as if shrouded in clouds.
MID_EV12_050_m01_019: <ACA>Here it lay, an entire continent, completely\nimpenetrable and unfathomable.
MID_EV12_050_m01_020: <ACA>But now the clouds are swept away—including why\nyou fear Vritra so.
MID_EV12_050_m01_021: <ACB>Fabio, you dismiss Chang'e's love as a whim, but can\nthat really be true?
MID_EV12_050_m01_022: <ACB>When Zenon says she's like a mother to them... That\nrings true to me.
MID_EV12_050_m01_023: <ACB>Sometimes a parent has to do whatever it takes to\nprotect a child.
MID_EV12_050_m01_024: <ACB>And they'll do it, without regrets, no matter how\nmuch they suffer for it.
MID_EV12_050_m01_025: <ACB>I'm a mother. I understand.
MID_EV12_050_m01_026: <ACB>That's just how it is for parents. I'm sure Chang'e is\na wonderful parent to these people.
MID_EV12_050_m01_027: <ACB>As you say. If she had not protected us, we would\nbe long gone by now.
MID_EV12_050_m01_028: <ACB>Tch...
MID_EV12_050_m01_029: Still, the ship is in far worse a state than I had\nanticipated. I am sorely disappointed.
MID_EV12_050_m01_030: So much of its structure has simply been lost. There\nis no salvaging it. It's just scrap.
MID_EV12_050_m01_031: What did you say? Are you calling our home scrap?
MID_EV12_050_m01_032: I have a proposal. If you accede to it, I will postpone\nmy report to Vritra.
MID_EV12_050_m01_033: Wha... What?
MID_EV12_050_m01_034: You must return the Grand Megaliths of Dagda—\nto me.
MID_EV12_050_m01_035: If I can bring them back under Agarthan control, I\nwill be commended. My star will rise.
MID_EV12_050_m01_036: What say you? It seems cheap at the price.
MID_EV12_050_m01_037: No. That is not something I can do.
MID_EV12_050_m01_038: You must seek out our Mediator. We have entrusted\nKunlun to her.
MID_EV12_050_m01_039: She is the one who can agree to your bargain.
MID_EV12_050_m01_040: The Mediator? I believe I know what you refer to.
MID_EV12_050_m01_041: A synthetic human with perfect intelligence and\noutstanding physical capability.
MID_EV12_050_m01_042: One designed to resolve all problems a ship may\nencounter. I never conceived I might meet one.
MID_EV12_050_m01_043: But in fact, I most likely already have.
MID_EV12_050_m01_044: Visitor from Agartha, we will pray for your success.